Ladybird scrolls the beginning of a find-in-page match into view. The
other engines also scroll the match’s own geometry, not an element
around it: Blink’s TextFinder scrolls the match’s Range::BoundingBox()
in ScrollToVisible(), WebKit’s FrameSelection::revealSelection() shows
the selected match, and Gecko’s nsTypeAheadFind::FindItNow() calls
ScrollSelectionIntoView() on the selection it makes of the match.
